          <article class="bdc__feature"><h4>3. Recovery-Focused Programs</h4><p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Gives the chair a routine-based feel for active lifestyle use.</p><p><strong>Demo cue:</strong> Compare one recovery-style program against a standard relaxation sequence.</p></article>
          <article class="bdc__feature"><h4>4. Warm Up, Cool Down, Stretch, and Compression Sessions</h4><p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Creates a structured session flow instead of random full-body movement.</p><p><strong>Demo cue:</strong> Notice whether the sequence matches how you would actually use the chair before or after activity.</p></article>
          <article class="bdc__feature"><h4>5. Focused Sessions for Neck and Shoulders, Low Back, Glutes, and IT Bands</h4><p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Helps you start with the areas that matter most to your routine.</p><p><strong>Demo cue:</strong> Try the area you care about most and check roller alignment.</p></article>
          <article class="bdc__feature"><h4>6. Heated Rollers</h4><p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Adds warmth at the moving contact point.</p><p><strong>Demo cue:</strong> Notice whether heat makes deeper pressure feel smoother and more comfortable.</p></article>
